 "lines": [
  "Their Christmas tree went up in seconds.",
  "It had been up since Thanksgiving. Nobody had watered it in weeks.",
  "@af_heart: \"Kai, the lights are smoking!\"",
  "Lights and wiring play a part in more than two in five tree fires.",
  "A watered tree can shrug off a small flame. A dry one can't.",
  "In fire lab tests, dry trees were fully ablaze in under thirty seconds.",
  "@am_michael: \"Leave it! Everybody out, now!\"",
  "In about a [minute](minnit), the room can flash over. Everything in it bursts into flame.",
  "At the ceiling, it can top a thousand degrees. About twice as hot as an oven.",
  "Thirty years ago, families had about seventeen minutes to escape a house fire.",
  "Today, with modern furniture, it can be closer to three.",
  "@af_heart: \"Wait. Where's Leo?\"",
  "Leo was upstairs, asleep, and the smoke was rising fast.",
  "In house fires, smoke kills more people than the flames do.",
  "But Leo had done one thing right. He had shut his bedroom door.",
  "In tests, closed rooms stayed under a hundred degrees. Open ones passed a thousand.",
  "The smoke alarm woke him. Firefighters got him out his window.",
  "@am_echo: \"I'm okay! The door saved me!\"",
  "Here's the twist. More than a third of Christmas tree fires happen in January.",
  "By then, a lot of trees are bone dry.",
  "So water it every day, keep it three feet from heat, and turn the lights off at night.",
  "Skip that, and this is how fast it goes."
 ],
